# Copy to deploy/cloudrun.env (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Used by deploy/cloudrun-deploy.sh. CI can instead map GitHub Actions secrets
# into the job environment (see .github/workflows/cloudrun-deploy.yml).

# --- GCP ---
GCP_PROJECT=selfreminder-rnix
GCP_REGION=asia-south1
AR_REPO=webcast
SERVICE_NAME=webcast-api
IMAGE_NAME=webcast-api

# --- Required for a live Cloud Run service ---
# Prefer Supabase for production (see deploy/SUPABASE.md). Always use sslmode=require.
#
# Session pooler :5432 (recommended — IPv4 + full sessions for migrate/pgx):
#   postgres://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:SECRET@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Direct (often IPv6-only on newer projects):
#   postgres://postgres:SECRET@db.<PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Transaction pooler (RECOMMENDED for production queries; see deploy/SUPABASE.md
# "Connection budget"). The API detects :6543, switches pgx off named prepared
# statements, and keeps LISTEN + migrations on a session connection:
#   postgres://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:SECRET@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Legacy Cloud SQL unix socket (leave CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE set if you use this):
#   postgres://USER:PASS@/webcast?host=/cloudsql/PROJECT:REGION:INSTANCE&sslmode=disable
DATABASE_URL=

# Session-mode URL for the realtime LISTEN connection and boot migrations.
# Optional: defaults to DATABASE_URL, and for a Supabase :6543 DATABASE_URL the
# :5432 session pooler on the same host is used automatically.
#   postgres://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:SECRET@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_LISTEN_URL=

# session | transaction. Empty = inferred (:6543 → transaction). Setting
# "transaction" with a Supabase :5432 DATABASE_URL sends queries to :6543.
# DATABASE_POOL_MODE=

# Pool knobs (defaults in api/internal/store/dbconfig.go):
# DB_MAX_CONNS=            # 4 session mode, 6 transaction mode
# DB_MIN_CONNS=0
# DB_MAX_CONN_IDLE_TIME=60s
# DB_MAX_CONN_LIFETIME=30m
# DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=90s   # boot retries a full pooler this long
# DB_POOLER_POOL_SIZE=30   # Supabase session pool_size, for the boot budget check

# Session cookie signing key: >=32 random bytes. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
SESSION_SECRET=

# LiveKit — prefer LIVEKIT_PROJECTS JSON; legacy LIVEKIT_* still works for one project.
# LIVEKIT_PROJECTS=[{"id":"default","url":"wss://YOUR.livekit.cloud","api_key":"...","api_secret":"..."}]
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
# LIVEKIT_HTTP_URL=   # optional; defaults from LIVEKIT_URL

# --- Admin bootstrap (optional; required on a fresh DB with no operators) ---
# Comma-separated emails. Password must be ≥ MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH (10 in production).
# On API boot, EnsureAdminAccount creates missing accounts; PromoteAdmins reconciles is_admin.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=ops@example.com
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-at-least-10-chars

# --- Production knobs (script sets sensible defaults if omitted) ---
APP_ENV=production
COOKIE_SECURE=true
RECORDINGS_ENABLED=false
SEED_DEV=false

# --- Recording storage (only read when RECORDINGS_ENABLED=true) ---
# "disk" needs nothing further. "s3" is an S3-compatible bucket — Cloudflare R2
# preferred (free egress); Backblaze B2 still works — and needs all five
# RECORDINGS_S3_* below; config.go refuses to boot without them.
# RECORDINGS_BACKEND=s3
#
# R2: bucket in the Cloudflare dashboard, S3 API token (Object Read & Write),
# endpoint https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com, region auto.
# Custom domain recordings.webinarliv.com on that bucket; CORS GET from
# https://webinarliv.com. Cache .ts/.mp4; bypass .m3u8.
#
# B2 (legacy): scoped application key (listFiles, readFiles, writeFiles,
# deleteFiles) — never the account master key.
# RECORDINGS_S3_BUCKET=webinar-recordings-prod
# RECORDINGS_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# RECORDINGS_S3_REGION=auto
# RECORDINGS_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# RECORDINGS_S3_SECRET_KEY=
#
# --- LiveKit Egress & Cloudflare CDN (Server-side recording) ---
# RECORDINGS_MODE=egress       # "egress" (server-side via LiveKit Egress) or "client" (browser canvas)
# RECORDINGS_EGRESS_TEMPLATE_URL=https://webinarliv.com/recorder-template  # Custom Zoom-style layout template
# RECORDINGS_EGRESS_PRESET=720p  # "720p" (default since 29 Oct 2026) or "1080p"
# RECORDINGS_CDN_BASE_URL=https://recordings.webinarliv.com  # public host for .mp4 / HLS; browsers must not hit the bucket origin
# RECORDINGS_RETENTION_DAYS=30  # auto-delete cloud recordings after this many days (0 = keep forever)
# MEDIA_QUOTA_DEFAULT_MB=10  # WhatsApp media library space per host (admins can override per account)
#
# Live attendee origin (MediaMTX on the box). Both or neither. Egress RTMP is localhost
# because Egress and MediaMTX share host networking on the box. BROADCAST_HLS_BASE is the
# fallback for a LiveKit project without its own broadcastHlsBase: the box's own address.
# Viewers in EDGE_NEAR_COUNTRIES play it directly; everyone else plays EDGE_PLAYBACK_BASE
# (the Bunny pull zone) or the project's edgePlaybackBase (docs/edge-delivery.md).
# BROADCAST_RTMP_BASE=rtmp://127.0.0.1:1935/live
# BROADCAST_HLS_BASE=https://203.0.113.10.sslip.io/live
# How far behind live the player sits, per path (docs/edge-delivery.md). Default 3; 1.5–6.
# EDGE_TARGET_LATENCY_SEC=3
# EDGE_TARGET_LATENCY_CDN_SEC=5

# End a live webinar that nobody has been in for this many minutes, once its
# scheduled start has passed. Covers the host who closes the tab instead of
# pressing End. 0 turns the sweep off.
# EMPTY_ROOM_CLOSE_MIN=10
#
# --- Email (optional). Without SMTP_HOST, invitations stay in the outbox as skipped. ---
# The host is not hardcoded. Production is Gmail:
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USERNAME is the Gmail address.
#   SMTP_PASSWORD is a Google app password (the account must have 2FA). A normal
#   Gmail password is rejected. This client speaks SMTP AUTH, not OAuth.
# SMTP_FROM must be that same account, or a verified "Send mail as" alias. Gmail
# rewrites or rejects any other From. A display name is fine:
#   SMTP_FROM=Webinar Liv <you@gmail.com>
# Per-host addresses (gsp@webinarliv.com) are Reply-To only. Do not put them in
# SMTP_FROM. Mail whose From is @webinarliv.com but which Gmail actually sends will
# fail SPF alignment: the domain's SPF is "v=spf1 include:spf.spacemail.com ~all"
# and does not authorize Gmail. Keeping From on the Gmail address avoids that.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=you@gmail.com
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=help@example.com
#
# Welcome email: one thank-you to every new account (signup form or first Google
# sign-in), sent through the same outbox. On by default; WELCOME_EMAIL=false turns it
# off. CONTACT_* are the "reach us" details it shows.
# WELCOME_EMAIL=true
# CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@webinarliv.com
# CONTACT_PHONE=+91-9852411280
# POST /telemetry and the token-issuance timing log, for a performance-test
# window — temporary, off by default. See web/lib/telemetry.ts.
TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false
# AV1 publishing in the browser: off (default) | meetings | on. Served to every client via
# /api/config and read before the room's first publish, so flipping it needs no web deploy:
#   gcloud run services update webcast-api --region <region> --update-env-vars AV1_PUBLISH=off
# (and set the GitHub variable AV1_PUBLISH so the next deploy keeps it). "on" never applies
# to edge webinars: the mix's egress Chrome cannot take AV1. See web/lib/codec-policy.ts.
AV1_PUBLISH=off
# Comma-separated origins are OK — deploy script uses --env-vars-file (not
# comma-joined --set-env-vars), so multiple origins do not break gcloud parsing.
CORS_ORIGINS=https://YOUR_FRONTEND_ORIGIN
WEB_BASE_URL=https://YOUR_FRONTEND_ORIGIN
APP_NAME=Webinar Liv

# --- Supabase Auth (Google sign-in) — optional; password login works without these ---
# Project Settings → API. JWT Secret never goes to the browser.
# See deploy/SUPABASE.md § Auth — Google via Supabase.
# Browser Auth origin (custom domain once live; otherwise the project URL).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://auth.webinarliv.com
# Project *.supabase.co origin — JWT iss / JWKS fallback after the custom domain.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...anon
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# Google One Tap / Drive — public Web client ID from selfreminder-rnix
# (same client as Supabase Auth → Google). Exposed via /api/config as googleClientId.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=123456789-xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=   # optional; Drive Picker only
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=   # Web OAuth client secret. Required for Connect YouTube
#                         # (creates lives via YouTube Data API). Add authorized
#                         # redirect URI: {WEB_BASE_URL}/api/host/youtube/callback
#                         # Enable YouTube Data API v3 on the GCP project.

# Connect WhatsApp — Meta Embedded Signup. All three or none; the API refuses to
# boot on a partial set. Each host connects their own WhatsApp Business Account
# and Meta bills them for conversations, so these only identify the app.
# See docs/WHATSAPP-CRM-PLAN.md for the Meta-side prerequisites.
# META_APP_ID=              # public; the browser opens the signup dialog with it
# META_APP_SECRET=          # server-only: signs the exchange, verifies webhooks
# META_WHATSAPP_CONFIG_ID=  # the Embedded Signup configuration's id
# META_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=  # must match the Meta app's webhook Verify token,
#                             # with the callback at {API}/api/webhooks/whatsapp

# Razorpay — self-serve plans: Buy on /pricing turns hosting on once paid.
# Key id and secret together or neither; the API refuses to boot on one alone.
# Start with TEST keys (rzp_test_…) from dashboard.razorpay.com → Account &
# Settings → API Keys. The webhook secret is the one you type when adding a
# webhook (Settings → Webhooks) at {API}/api/webhooks/razorpay with the events
# payment.captured and order.paid. Prices live in api/internal/billing/billing.go.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# BILLING_GST_PERCENT=18      # added to INR prices at checkout; 0 for none
#
# The 7-day free trial on monthly plans needs the keys above AND this salt, which
# keeps the trial once per person (phone/email/payment method are stored only as
# salted hashes). Generate it ONCE: openssl rand -hex 32. Never change it — every
# earlier trial would stop matching and could be taken again. Unset: no trials;
# the pricing page offers pay-now only. Also enable Subscriptions in Razorpay and
# add the subscription.* events to the webhook above.
# TRIAL_HASH_SALT=

# Connect Zoom — per-host OAuth. All four of id, secret, redirect, and token
# key, or the card stays "Zoom is not configured". The webhook secret is
# optional for Connect; without it POST /api/webhooks/zoom refuses the body.
# See docs/zoom-app-checklist.md.
# ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=
# ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ZOOM_REDIRECT_URL=https://webinarliv.com/api/host/zoom/callback
# ZOOM_TOKEN_KEY=             # openssl rand -base64 32
# ZOOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=        # Zoom app Secret Token for event subscriptions

# Background job while scaled to zero. With --min-instances 0 no goroutine runs between
# requests, so reminders, drips, bots and meeting limits would wait for the next visitor.
# Set this, deploy, then run deploy/cloud-scheduler-tick.sh once: Cloud Scheduler then
# POSTs /api/internal/tick every minute with it. At least 32 characters.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# TICK_SECRET=

# Web Push: "Get a notification when it starts", the host's lobby and recap alerts, and the
# installable app's notifications. All three or none (a partial set refuses to boot); unset,
# the UI offers no notifications. Generate the key pair once — changing it later orphans every
# existing browser subscription:
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:support@webinarliv.com

# Native push to the Android and iOS apps (Firebase Cloud Messaging HTTP v1; FCM reaches iOS
# through the APNs key uploaded into the Firebase project). A Firebase service account's JSON key
# (Project settings, Service accounts, Generate new private key), on one line or base64. Unset,
# the apps' tokens are stored and nothing is sent to them. See apps/mobile/README.md.
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Or, preferred on Cloud Run (29 Oct 2026), no key at all: the Firebase project ID. The API takes
# its FCM token from the metadata server for the runtime service account, which needs
# roles/firebasecloudmessaging.admin on the project. FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON wins when both are
# set; neither, native sending is off.
# FCM_PROJECT_ID=selfreminder-rnix

# Server-side live captions (deploy/captions/README.md). The same value goes in the caption
# agent's CAPTIONS_SECRET (each video box's worker gets it in its user data, as the captions box
# did). Unset, the
# internal caption endpoints do not exist and captions stay on-device. At least 32 characters.
# CAPTIONS_SECRET=
# CAPTIONS_AGENT_NAME=webinar-captions

# Cloud recording of edge webinars from the audience mix, with no second compositor
# (deploy/livekit-box/README.md, "Recording from the mix"). The same value goes in the SFU
# box's /opt/livekit/.env as MIXREC_SECRET. Needs RECORDINGS_BACKEND=s3 (the recorder uploads
# through a URL the API signs). The recorder is found at the live origin with /live replaced by
# /mixrec; MIXREC_URL (or a project's mixRecorderUrl in LIVEKIT_PROJECTS) overrides that.
# Unset: an edge recording starts its own compositor. At least 32 characters.
# MIXREC_SECRET=
# MIXREC_URL=

# The on-demand DigitalOcean video server (deploy/digitalocean/README.md): the API creates the
# box's droplet when a session on SFU_BOX_PROJECT needs it and deletes it when idle. Both set to
# turn it on; DO_API_TOKEN is a secret (droplets, snapshots, volumes, reserved IPs: read/write).
# SFU_BOX_ALWAYS_ON=true keeps the box up whatever the demand (the rollback). The rest default to
# the values in that README.
# DO_API_TOKEN=
# SFU_BOX_PROJECT=do-blr
# SFU_BOX_ALWAYS_ON=false
# SFU_BOX_WARM_LEAD=15m
# SFU_BOX_IDLE_GRACE=40m
# SFU_BOX_BOOT_TIMEOUT=12m
# SFU_BOX_MAX_FAILURES=3
# SFU_BOX_NAME=sfu-blr-1
# SFU_BOX_REGION=blr1
# SFU_BOX_SIZE=c-4
# SFU_BOX_SNAPSHOT_TAG=webinar-sfu-image
# SFU_BOX_VOLUME=sfu-data
# SFU_BOX_RESERVED_IP=152.42.156.192
# SFU_BOX_TAGS=webinar-sfu
# SFU_BOX_SSH_KEYS=
# SFU_BOX_PARK_DROPLET=ops-blr-1
# SFU_BOX_TURN_HOST=
# The pool (deploy/digitalocean/README.md "More video servers"): this box's area and capacity in
# points, the further boxes declared ahead, and the capacity model. Unset is the one box above.
# SFU_BOX_AREA=in
# SFU_BOX_CAPACITY=100
# SFU_BOX_SLOTS=[{"project":"do-blr-2","name":"sfu-blr-2","volume":"sfu-data-2","reservedIp":"<ip>"}]
# SFU_BOX_POINTS={"mix":20,"extra":10,"viewersPerPoint":10,"meetingBase":4,"meetingBaseSize":10,"meetingPeoplePerPoint":2,"simulive":0}
# Grafana Cloud for the box's Alloy (deploy/livekit-box/README.md, "Grafana Cloud"): the API
# passes these in every new droplet's user data and sfu-boot.sh writes them into the volume's .env,
# so the box reports metrics and logs from first boot. All five or none (the API refuses a partial
# set while SFU_BOX_PROJECT is set). GRAFANA_CLOUD_TOKEN is a secret: a metrics:write + logs:write
# access policy token, nothing more (anything on the box can read its user data).
# GRAFANA_CLOUD_PROM_URL=
# GRAFANA_CLOUD_PROM_USER=
# GRAFANA_CLOUD_LOKI_URL=
# GRAFANA_CLOUD_LOKI_USER=
# GRAFANA_CLOUD_TOKEN=
# Who transcribes server captions (with CAPTIONS_SECRET). deepgram, the default when
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY is set: a light worker on each video box (deploy/livekit-box,
# docker-compose.captions-worker.yml) streams the stage speakers' microphones to Deepgram Nova-3
# only while they speak, and its finals are the session transcript. The API passes the key and
# the rest to each droplet in its user data. local, the default without a key: the old captions box.
# CAPTIONS_PROVIDER=
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# CAPTIONS_DEEPGRAM_MODEL=nova-3
# Only the worker's fallback now: each webinar names its captions language.
# CAPTIONS_DEEPGRAM_LANGUAGE=multi
# The captions language a new webinar starts with (a code from api/types/captions_language.go:
# en-IN, hi, multi, ta, te, kn, mr, bn, gu, ml). Hosts change it per webinar and in the room.
# CAPTIONS_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE=en-IN
# CAPTIONS_API_URL=https://webinarliv.com
# The captions box (deploy/digitalocean/README.md, "Captions box"): a droplet made and deleted with
# the video box that runs the Whisper caption agent. Retired from production on 2026-10-27, kept
# as the fallback: made only with CAPTIONS_BOX_ENABLED=true AND CAPTIONS_PROVIDER=local set
# explicitly (and CAPTIONS_SECRET and the box manager). The deploy workflow passes it from the
# CAPTIONS_BOX_ENABLED_OVERRIDE variable. CPUS defaults to the size's vCPUs and MAX_ROOMS to one
# room per two vCPUs (at least 1).
# CAPTIONS_BOX_ENABLED=false
# CAPTIONS_BOX_SIZE=s-4vcpu-8gb
# CAPTIONS_BOX_IMAGE=webinar-captions-image
# CAPTIONS_BOX_NAME=captions-blr-1
# CAPTIONS_BOX_TAGS=webinar-captions
# CAPTIONS_BOX_CPUS=
# CAPTIONS_BOX_MAX_ROOMS=
# CAPTIONS_BOX_MODEL=base.en
# CAPTIONS_BOX_API_URL=https://webinarliv.com
# CAPTIONS_BOX_LIVEKIT_URL=
# CAPTIONS_BOX_BOOT_TIMEOUT=10m

# Optional: Cloud SQL only. Leave unset when DATABASE_URL points at Supabase.
# CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE=ai-project-490516:asia-south1:webcast

# OpenTelemetry: traces, request metrics and logs to Grafana Cloud over OTLP/HTTP
# (api/internal/observe). Entirely off while OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is unset: no
# exporter, no wrapping, nothing sent. Stdout logging to Cloud Logging is unchanged either way.
#
# Endpoint: Grafana Cloud portal -> your stack -> OpenTelemetry -> Configure. It looks like
#   https://otlp-gateway-prod-<region>.grafana.net/otlp   (no /v1/traces suffix)
# Headers: a SECRET. "Authorization=Basic " + base64("<instance id>:<access policy token>"),
# the token needing metrics:write, logs:write and traces:write. Build it locally:
#   printf 'Authorization=Basic %s' "$(printf '%s:%s' "$GRAFANA_INSTANCE_ID" "$GRAFANA_TOKEN" | base64 | tr -d '\n')"
# and store it as the GitHub secret OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS (the deploy workflow passes it
# through), never in a committed file.
#
# OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES defaults (in cloudrun-deploy.sh) to
#   deployment.environment=prod,deployment.environment.name=prod,service.version=<commit short sha>
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER defaults to parentbased_traceidratio with OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG 0.2.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=webcast-api
# OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.2
